meta {
  name: Providers - Update
  type: http
  seq: 31
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/super-admin/v1/models/providers/:provider
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{superAdminToken}}
}

params:path {
  provider: openai
}

body:json {
  {
    "byok_enabled": false,
    "disabled_message": "OpenAI keys are paused for a cost review. Back soon.",
    "notify": "email",
    "reason": "Cost review for customer OpenAI keys",
    "totp_code": "123456"
  }
}

docs {
  The switches for customers' own keys for one provider. Any of: `byok_enabled` (customers can add and use their own key; off hides it and keeps existing keys unused), `connect_enabled` (one-click connect; null for the config default), `featured`, `sort_order`, `free_tier_note`, `disabled_message`.

  Always needs a reason. Turning `byok_enabled` off also needs a fresh `totp_code`. When customer keys are switched off or back on, `notify` says whether to tell the workspaces that have a key: `none` (default), `in_app`, or `email` (in-app and email). Switching raises an alert.
}
